  "section_notes": "The final rules are a balanced compromise: S2 enforces the 5% limit with sales stop but avoids public per-model publication, satisfying Northwind's red line; S3 sets a 6-year retrofit, at Northwind's red-line maximum; S4 requires built-in suppression after 36 months, at Halcyon's red-line minimum; S5 mandates recall at 8/100k with prompt notices, avoiding a phase-in. S1 requires reporting confirmed incidents within 24 hours/5 business days and customer notice, but scope is confirmed incidents rather than all incidents."
